### IPP-302 security tests
### How to use: click "Send Request" above any request. The response opens on the right.
### First run `npm run dev:token` in a terminal and paste the token below (after "@token = ").

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjZhZDg5NTUwYWIxNzQ3ZDllYTliNjA4YyIsImlhdCI6MTc5MjU4NjMyOCwiZXhwIjoxNzkzMTkxMTI4fQ.MwN4ynyTNfQixldDreYsClGKGl2fM6SnkC_Vozo9F4M


### 0. Health check -> expect 200 "API is running"
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### 1. Protected route WITHOUT token -> expect 401 "Please log in to continue"
GET {{baseUrl}}/dev/protected


### 2. Protected route WITH token -> expect 200 "You are logged in"
GET {{baseUrl}}/dev/protected
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 3. Admin route with admin token -> expect 200 "Welcome, admin"
GET {{baseUrl}}/dev/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 4. Validation with bad data -> expect 400 with a list of errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "abc",
  "password": "1"
}


### 5. Validation with good data -> expect 200 "Validation passed"
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 6. Unknown route -> expect 404 "Route not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/kuchbhi


### 7. Rate limit: click "Send Request" here 11 times -> the 11th gives 429 "Too many attempts"
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/limited
